From 3f7f89c6b5e1adc02835e4313d24fafbc4bc5ffc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:43:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: platform: add the HiSTB JPEG decoder driver

The HiSTB JPEG decoder has no mainline driver. The block decodes one
baseline picture per mem2mem job into 4:2:0 semi-planar YUV with Cr
first, and reports an engine error for inputs it cannot take. Add a V4L2
mem2mem driver that parses the header in the kernel, expands the
quantiser and Huffman tables into the forms the block expects, shifts
canonical codes over unused code lengths, and names the refusals:
non-canonical sampling factors and scans carrying restart markers. A
drained session with no picture left to decode ends inside the command
itself, so the end of stream is announced by the mem2m core, the
completing capture buffer is flagged last, and clients can subscribe to
the end-of-stream event.

The vendor directory under drivers/media/platform is added here, ahead
of the other media drivers of this family, with the platform Kconfig and
Makefile hooks and the decoder's own symbol and object line.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
